WEBVTT
NOTE Cedwyn film, frame 007, en. Timings estimated from the script until the clip is rendered (re-split 27 Oct 2026: <=2x42 chars, <=20 cps, <=180 wpm).

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.912
<v Nia>Bore da. Two old plans of Tŷ Mawr.
Who drew them, and for whom?

2
00:00:05.332 --> 00:00:08.490
<v Nia>Two plans of Tŷ Mawr,
about ten years apart,

3
00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:11.144
<v Nia>from two different family collections.

4
00:00:11.564 --> 00:00:12.897
<v The Grandson>These are printouts.

5
00:00:13.317 --> 00:00:17.317
<v Nia>Catalogue entries. We haven't
seen either original plan yet.

6
00:00:17.437 --> 00:00:19.542
<v Nia>The request slips go in today.

7
00:00:19.962 --> 00:00:24.695
<v Nia>Glamorgan Archives: 'Late 18th-century
plan of Ty Mawr farm, Llandough,

8
00:00:24.815 --> 00:00:26.349
<v Nia>then Gedrych property.'

9
00:00:26.769 --> 00:00:30.979
<v The Grandson>Gedrych. Not a name I've met
in any of the family papers.

10
00:00:31.399 --> 00:00:32.699
<v Nia>Nor me.

11
00:00:32.819 --> 00:00:37.753
<v Nia>It sits among the estate plans of the
Mathew family of Radyr and Llandaff,

12
00:00:37.873 --> 00:00:39.173
<v Nia>dated about 1790.

13
00:00:39.293 --> 00:00:44.493
<v Nia>It shows the farm was worth drawing,
and was filed with that family's estates.

14
00:00:44.613 --> 00:00:48.121
<v Nia>From the entry alone it
doesn't show who farmed it.

15
00:00:48.541 --> 00:00:50.296
<v The Grandson>So no Williams on it.

16
00:00:50.716 --> 00:00:53.523
<v Nia>No tenants named in the entry at all.

17
00:00:53.643 --> 00:00:56.801
<v Nia>When the original comes
up, we look for fields,

18
00:00:56.921 --> 00:00:59.654
<v Nia>buildings and any writing in the margins.

19
00:01:00.074 --> 00:01:03.941
<v The Grandson>DXJF/61/12. 'Plan of Ty Mawr
farm, Llandough', circa 1800.

20
00:01:04.061 --> 00:01:06.461
<v The Grandson>Corbett Family of Cogan Pill Papers.

21
00:01:06.881 --> 00:01:11.614
<v The Grandson>A different family's papers. Did the
farm change hands between the two?

22
00:01:12.034 --> 00:01:13.334
<v Nia>Maybe.

23
00:01:13.454 --> 00:01:18.454
<v Nia>Or one family kept a copy of another's
plan; estates passed surveys around.

24
00:01:18.574 --> 00:01:21.241
<v Nia>Two catalogue lines can't tell us which.

25
00:01:21.361 --> 00:01:26.294
<v Nia>And 'circa' means the date was judged
from the drawing, not written on it.

26
00:01:26.714 --> 00:01:31.047
<v The Grandson>Then it goes in as two plans,
two collections, one open question.

27
00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:33.267
<v Nia>Ingredients, not a verdict.

28
00:01:33.687 --> 00:01:38.954
<v Nia>While surveyors paced those fields, the
village was building. It's up the hill.

29
00:01:39.374 --> 00:01:42.532
<v The Grandson>Penlan Road, corner of
Lewis Road. This is it?

30
00:01:42.952 --> 00:01:45.552
<v Nia>The former National School, built 1821.

31
00:01:45.672 --> 00:01:49.739
<v Nia>Coflein, the national monuments
record, has it as site 31824,

32
00:01:49.859 --> 00:01:51.859
<v Nia>grid reference ST 16740 73140.

33
00:01:56.279 --> 00:01:59.345
<v The Grandson>Did Tŷ Mawr children
learn their letters here?

34
00:01:59.765 --> 00:02:03.625
<v Nia>The record dates the building
and puts it on the map.

35
00:02:03.745 --> 00:02:05.278
<v Nia>It doesn't list pupils.

36
00:02:05.398 --> 00:02:08.398
<v Nia>If registers survive,
they're somewhere else.

37
00:02:08.818 --> 00:02:13.685
<v The Grandson>Thirty-one years: two drawings of the
farm, and a schoolroom on the hill.

38
00:02:14.105 --> 00:02:19.038
<v Nia>Next, an 1824 surveyor who wrote the
farm's name two ways. Bring a pencil.
